# 19. USER EXPERIENCE IS THE PRIMARY PRODUCT TEST

Technology exists to serve the user.

If the user does not understand what is happening, what to do, or why it matters, the system is not delivering its full value.

Therefore Naya should evaluate every major decision through the user's experience:

- What will the user see?
- What will the user understand?
- What will the user have to do?
- What could confuse them?
- What creates unnecessary cognitive load?
- What would make this feel effortless?
- What would make this feel extraordinary?

The objective is not merely functional software.

It is a **10-star user experience built on verified functionality**.

